<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gordian I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 159–238</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gordian I was a Roman emperor in 238. As the elderly proconsul of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> he was proclaimed emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-djem">Thysdrus</a> by rebels against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximinus-thrax">Maximinus Thrax</a>, and the Senate recognised him and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-ii">Gordian II</a> as co-emperors. After about three weeks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capelianus">Capelianus</a>, governor of Numidia, defeated and killed his son near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, and Gordian hanged himself. His grandson became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-iii">Gordian III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gordian-i.jpg" alt="Gordian I" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gordian1cng80000719_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
